.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt NC 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm nc
.Nd connect to or listen on TCP and UDP ports
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl u
.Op Fl w Ar seconds
.Op Fl s Ar text
.Op Fl n Ar bytes
.Ar host port
.Nm
.Fl l
.Op Fl u
.Fl p Ar port
.Op Fl e
.Op Fl w Ar seconds
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
opens a
.Dq net:tcp/ Ns Ar host : Ns Ar port
or
.Dq net:udp/ Ns Ar host : Ns Ar port
socket through the native
.Dq net:
server. In client mode it connects (TCP) or sends a datagram (UDP), optionally writes the
.Fl s
payload once, and with
.Fl n
reads at most that many bytes and prints them. A UDP client must choose its local port with
.Fl b .
.Pp
In listen mode
.Fl l
requires
.Fl p Ar port .
TCP uses
.Dv LISTEN / ACCEPT ; UDP uses
.Dv BIND . With
.Fl e
the listener echoes one received message back to the sender and exits. Every operation is
bounded by
.Fl w
(seconds, default 5); a refused connection, timeout or malformed option exits non-zero.
.Pp
The tool uses only the
.Dq net:
scheme API; it never opens a raw socket and never touches a NIC address.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ifconfig 8 ,
.Xr netd 8
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD.
